\f0\fs24 \cf2 Come closer and observe the frieze running along the center of the piano. Does it seem like just a decoration? In reality, it\'92s much more. It\'92s a window into the Renaissance, reinvented with 19th-century sensitivity and taste. Inspired by the grotesques of the 16th-century choir at San Giovanni in Parma, this frieze is not a copy, but a free interpretation signed by the Bagatti Valsecchi brothers. The photographs preserved in the archive tell the story of the origin of this motif, but what you see here is the result of a refined adaptation. Everything has been redesigned to harmonize with the style of the house, to blend seamlessly with the surroundings, and to convey an idea of beauty that is never mere nostalgia, but creative rediscovery.\
A small masterpiece that reminds us that tradition and innovation are not opposites, but two souls of the same vision.}